        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test: migrate raw mkdtemp to withTempDir in embedded-agent-runner and compaction tests",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- Migrate 4 test files in `src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/` and `src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe/` from raw `fs.mkdtemp`/`fs.mkdtempSync` to auto-cleaning `withTempDir` helper\r\n- Removes 15 bare `mkdtemp` calls that had no cleanup, preventing temp directory leaks on disk\r\n- Part of the ongoing temp-dir migration (#96711)\r\n\r\n## Background\r\n\r\nThese test files used raw `fs.mkdtemp`/`fs.mkdtempSync` without any `rm`/`rmSync` cleanup, causing temp directories to persist on disk after test runs. The project standardized on `withTempDir`/`withTempDirSync`/`createSuiteTempRootTracker` helpers from `src/test-helpers/temp-dir.ts` which provide automatic cleanup.\r\n\r\n## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\n4 files with 15 bare `mkdtemp` calls and no cleanup:\r\n\r\n| File | Calls | Strategy |\r\n|------|-------|----------|\r\n| `attempt.cwd-split.test.ts` | 1 | `withTempDir` wrap |\r\n| `attempt.spawn-workspace.context-engine.test.ts` | 1 | `withTempDir` wrap |\r\n| `transcript-rewrite.test.ts` | 2 | `withTempDir` wrap |\r\n| `compaction.test.ts` | 11 | `withTempDir` wrap per test |\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nEach test creates a temp directory with `fs.mkdtemp` and uses it for session stores or sandbox workspaces, but never cleans up. Moving to `withTempDir` ensures automatic cleanup after each test.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nNone — test-only change with no user-visible behavior impact.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n### Behavior addressed\r\n\r\nBare `fs.mkdtemp`/`fs.mkdtempSync` calls without cleanup in test files.\r\n\r\n### Environment\r\n\r\nLocal development, Node 22, Linux.\r\n\r\n### Commands and results\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n$ pnpm test \\\r\n  src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/attempt.cwd-split.test.ts \\\r\n  src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/attempt.spawn-workspace.context-engine.test.ts \\\r\n  src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/transcript-rewrite.test.ts \\\r\n  src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.compaction.test.ts\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n Test Files  4 passed (4)\r\n      Tests  87 passed (87)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Observed result\r\n\r\nAll 87 tests pass. Zero bare `mkdtemp`/`mkdtempSync` remaining in the 4 modified files.\r\n\r\nCleanup proof — `withTempDir` removes per-test subdirectories; shared prefix roots remain as empty shells (design decision — they are reused across tests with the same prefix):\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# Run compaction tests (11 withTempDir calls, each writes to session store)\r\n$ pnpm test src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.compaction.test.ts\r\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\r\n      Tests  11 passed (11)\r\n\r\n# Check: shared roots exist but are empty — no leaked test content\r\n$ for d in /tmp/openclaw-compaction-*/; do\r\n    if [ -n \"$(ls -A \"$d\" 2>/dev/null)\" ]; then echo \"LEAK: $d\"; fi\r\n  done\r\n# (no output — all roots are empty)\r\n\r\n# Each withTempDir cleans up `dir-N` in its `finally` block.\r\n# drainSessionStoreWriterQueuesForTest() is called before the callback\r\n# returns, so queued session-store writes complete before cleanup.\r\n```\r\n\r\n### What was not tested\r\n\r\nNo CI or cross-platform verification. The change is mechanical — each `fs.mkdtemp(...)` → `await withTempDir({...}, async (dir) => {...})`, with drain calls added where session-store reconciliation enqueues async writes.\r\n",
        "branch": "fix/gap-tempdir-batch04",
